WEBVTT

00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:18,040
Hello everybody, this is Dr. Connors and this Zoom session, this recording, it's going

00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:26,960
to be about a serious spiritual matter when we come to wanting to be healed, that I think

00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:35,560
we need to address and just keep our focus to make sure that we keep our focus on the right

00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:36,560
things.

00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:41,600
We all want healing when we're sick, we have cancer, we have serious disease, we have

00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:50,120
Lyme, we have ALS, Parkinson's and all sorts of problems in this world.

00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:55,480
And we can ask serious questions and I think you're called to do that.

00:00:55,480 --> 00:01:04,560
When we go through the grieving process of understanding that we are mortal and our life

00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:09,600
is not to be lived completely on this earth, it gets a little scary.

00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:13,800
But we're in our 20s we think we're going to live forever.

00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:21,480
And as we get older and we start having serious diagnoses then that reality hits in and many

00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:27,680
times we turn to God and that's a blessing, we're supposed to turn to God in times of crisis.

00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:32,880
But we have to be careful that we don't turn to God just to get what we want.

00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:39,680
Yes, we're supposed to ask for what we want and the Bible is very clear that you don't

00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:43,320
receive because you don't ask.

00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:49,000
But it's also very clear that we're supposed to ask with the right heart and we're supposed

00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,800
to accept God's answer.

00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:58,800
Paul made it very clear that he asked for his thorn of his side to be taken away three times,

00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:04,800
which I find it kind of funny because I probably ask for my thorns to be taken away

00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,800
575 times at least.

00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:15,800
And I don't fully understand that passage why he would only ask three times.

00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:21,800
But maybe it was three different periods of his life where he was intense prayer about whatever

00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:27,800
that thorn be, an illness, a deformity, whatever it is we don't know.

00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:32,800
He was intensely in prayer and got the answer from God that it wasn't going to be taken away

00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:37,800
and he let it go for a period of time and then took it up another period of time.

00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:42,800
And there's a time and a season for everything and we're called to do that and we need to be

00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:49,800
fervent in our prayer and fervent in our asking and I think we need to ask for healing.

00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:54,800
I'm praying for healing for all of you and for myself on a daily basis.

00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,800
But we have to keep it in balance.

00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:02,800
First of all, biblically is healing promised.

00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:08,800
We can pull up verses all through the Bible where healing was promised to a certain person,

00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:13,800
to a certain people group and to us as believers as whole.

00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:18,800
So healing is for us in the new covenant.

00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:23,800
God did come to heal all our wounds and all our diseases.

00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:27,800
We need that they're going to be healed this side of heaven.

00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:32,800
If that was true, every believer from the New Testament on would still be alive.

00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,800
And that's not true.

00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:38,800
All the apostles suffered and died for his sake.

00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:51,800
Many were brutally martyred and to think that we have the right to not go down that same pathway

00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:56,800
is pompous, arrogant and just absolutely foolish.

00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:06,800
If we want to serve our Savior, we need to be willing to die in the flesh just as our Savior did.

00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:15,800
Paul said, oh that I may encompass the same sufferings that my Lord Jesus did that he could know him more fully.

00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:20,800
And that's got to be our desire of our heart as well.

00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:27,800
Not that we run around by like vassacus wanting to be tortured for God.

00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:36,800
But if we're not willing to suffer for his namesake, we have to really question where we are with our relationship with him.

00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:44,800
Though we're supposed to ask for a healing and we're supposed to be prayed for healing and prayed for all the things that we need in our life,

00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:50,800
they cannot be more important than our relationship with him.

00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:56,800
And as I write in my book, Kids or Kid Kill You, if you're already dead,

00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:03,800
our first and foremost prayer has got to be asking God to put his desires in our heart.

00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,800
What do you want me to pray for, Lord?

00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:22,800
Maybe God's got me with this sickness so that I'll get out of my knees and get closer to him and ask him what he wants me to pray for instead of just praying selfish prayers.

00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:29,800
I'm always speaking for myself, this is just my walk and I can encourage you through my walk about telling you what to do.

00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,800
But I know that's how God deals with me.

00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:35,800
He gives me sufferings to break me.

00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:46,800
He gives me sufferings to deal with strongholds in my life so that I can turn it over to him more readily because I fall every day.

00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:49,800
I think I can do it myself every day.

00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:53,800
And through my sufferings is how I learn obedience.

00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:56,800
Through my struggles I learn obedience.

00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:01,800
And that's my prayer every day.

00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,800
Lord, what do you need me to pray for?

00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,800
What do you need me to do?

00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:06,800
How do you need me to pray?

00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:11,800
Who do you need me to ask for help for?

00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:14,800
Because this isn't about me.

00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,800
Life is not about me.

00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:23,800
Life is not about me being healthy and rollerblading when I'm 85 years old and living this wonderful life.

00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,800
What good is that?

00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:28,800
What's the importance of that?

00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:35,800
That is not supposed to be our God in our life and that's what we have to be careful about.

00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:40,800
We need to be asking, what is the will of God for me?

00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,800
God, what do you want for me to do?

00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:48,800
If I've surrendered myself to be His, it's not about me anymore.

00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,800
That's done.

00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,800
It's not about me anymore.

00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:56,800
I've surrendered myself to Him.

00:06:56,800 --> 00:07:02,800
And if I have truly surrendered myself to Him and it's a daily basis, it's a daily walk.

00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,800
I understand that.

00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,800
It doesn't just happen one second in time.

00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:08,800
That's what sanctification is all about.

00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:20,800
Is Him chiseling away the rough edges of me to mold me and shape me daily more to be like the image of His Son.

00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,800
And it's a painful process.

00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:26,800
And I need to be willing to go through that pain.

00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,800
It's easy to say that.

00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:33,800
But when I'm in the middle of that pain, I need to be reminded of that.

00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:36,800
So that is what the will of God is for me.

00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:43,800
Not for me to live to be 95 years old and have a wonderful life and have a 401k and be able to golf every day.

00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,800
It's wonderful if you could do that.

00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,800
Don't get me wrong.

00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,800
But you need to be asking, is that the will of God for me?

00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,800
How can I serve you?

00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:54,800
How can I get to the end to hear those faithful words?

00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,800
Well done.

00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,800
Good and faithful servant.

00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,800
That's my goal.

00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:02,800
And I hope that's your goal too.

00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,800
And that's where we have to be careful.

00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:11,800
And I have to say some sharp words because healing or anything else can be idolatry.

00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:18,800
If my whole focus in life is to get something from God, that's idolatry.

00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:21,800
And I know those are tough words.

00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:25,800
And I know that might slap somebody in the face, but let it.

00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:29,800
Our purpose has to be free from idolatry.

00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:33,800
Our purpose has to be Lord, I'm your tool.

00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:34,800
Use me.

00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:40,800
Whether you want to use me, whether you want to make me go through horrible things and suffer

00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:46,800
because somebody's watching me and somebody's going to be set free because of that,

00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:48,800
Lord let it be your will.

00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:52,800
I remember, I think I've told you this story before, we were missionaries down in Mexico

00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:59,800
for a short period of time, and we had went self-financed.

00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,800
So we sold everything that we had.

00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:04,800
This is back when we were in our early 30s.

00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:09,800
And we played it and stayed in three years.

00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:15,800
But to see the deed down there, we taught it a Bible school and an orphanage in Monterey, Mexico.

00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:18,800
And we ended up building a dormitory there.

00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:23,800
And I taught at the Bible school for a year the Covenant of God.

00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:30,800
And we also worked in the Shanty towns down in Mexico, in the borders,

00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:33,800
and in the Shanty towns in Monterey.

00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,800
And we used to go back with our suburban.

00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:37,800
We had four kids at the time.

00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:42,800
We used to drive back and we registered as missionaries with some wonderful organizations

00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,800
on the other side of the border.

00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:49,800
Monterey is about three and a half hours in from the border of Texas, South Texas.

00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:52,800
And we used to pick up about every weekend or every other week,

00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:57,800
and we used to pick up and load our suburban full of stuff that we were given by,

00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:04,800
feed the children, international, and things that they were given by different corporations

00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:09,800
and stuff that we could give away, and that we could be a blessing to the people of the Shanty towns.

00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:14,800
And we used to pull it into the Shanty towns with our truck, and I used to say with my broken Spanish,

00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:19,800
everybody lined up and we would share a message of Jesus Christ and we would give people things

00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:24,800
and we would go around to their little places and talk to them about the Lord as best we could.

00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:29,800
And they were also gracious because they were all want to be Americans,

00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,800
and so everybody was so kind to us.

00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:37,800
And we never felt even in the worst situations that we were threatened or we were a danger in any way

00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:38,800
that we probably were.

00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:41,800
We just trusted the Lord that was going to take care of us.

00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:48,800
But I remember coming back from there after we left after a little over a year we were down there,

00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:53,800
we just completely ran out of funds and we could not raise money to stay down there anymore,

00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,800
and we had really no choice but to come back.

00:10:55,800 --> 00:11:03,800
And my wife and two youngest had my father flew them back up from South Texas,

00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:07,800
and I was driving back with my two older daughters.

00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:13,800
They were their early teens or a little bit younger at the time.

00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,800
And we had nothing.

00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:19,800
We had zero money, not one pity left.

00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:25,800
And I was pulling our suburban and I had just enough gas money to get home.

00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:29,800
And we had redded a U-Haul, a little teeny U-Haul trailer.

00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:34,800
We were pulling that because we had purchased some mattresses and a bunk bed down there.

00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:39,800
We didn't want to give that up so we brought that back with us.

00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:44,800
So all our worldly possessions were in this suburban and this little U-Haul trailer.

00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:50,800
Pull it back and I just remember the girls were sleeping and I was just crying out to the Lord

00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,800
because we didn't have a job.

00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:57,800
I didn't have my car practice license that couldn't practice anymore.

00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:03,800
I had given that up and it was crying out to the Lord because I felt like

00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:11,800
the best we could describe all our work down there was that we were putting drops of water into a bucket that had no bottom.

00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,800
That's what I felt like.

00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:17,800
What did we do anything to make a difference?

00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:23,800
We toiled and worked day and night and I just felt like we didn't do anything to make a difference.

00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:30,800
And it was one of those moments that I felt like I really heard from the Holy Spirit directly to my heart.

00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:39,800
He said, if I would have had you do this all over again for just one person would you do it?

00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:54,800
And that was a ginormous slap in the face to me because it was a revelation that God would send his son to go to the cross for just me

00:12:54,800 --> 00:13:01,800
or just one person and suffer everything that he suffered to take on the sins of the world.

00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:10,800
For my salvation alone, if it was only for me, why wouldn't I do that for him for just one person?

00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:16,800
And it's just a revelation that it's not about me, it's not about my stuff, it's not about my purpose.

00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:27,800
And it's so easy, especially in America, to become so idolatrous, to things, and to thinking that we have the right to even health.

00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,800
Who says I have the right to health?

00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:36,800
What kind of warped sense of understanding is that?

00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,800
We have the right to health.

00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:42,800
It is by a miracle of God that I am breathing today.

00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:46,800
It is a miracle that my heart is beating.

00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,800
It is said to be thankful for that.

00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:54,800
I'm widened because, oh my gosh, I might have two months to live or eight months to live or two years to live.

00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:57,800
You could never have been promised two seconds to live.

00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:01,800
Praise God that he's given me today.

00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,800
And yet we worry so much about tomorrow.

00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:11,460
Jesus said to Peter, let the days own troubles be enough for today.

00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:14,460
And I need to learn that.

00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:22,460
The problem is, really, honestly, it's who we put our faith in, that makes a difference.

00:14:22,460 --> 00:14:26,460
The problem is, most of the time, I have my faith in a what?

00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:28,460
In me getting better, that's what my faith is.

00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:30,460
My faith is in me carrying cancer.

00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:34,460
My faith is in this right-fishing working or my nutrition working.

00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:37,460
My faith is in my relationships being good.

00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:44,460
My faith is that my 401K is still healthy and that the economy is going to stay up.

00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:47,460
That's the wrong thing to have our faith in.

00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:49,460
It's a faith in who?

00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:54,130
That's who we have to have our faith in.

00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:58,130
It's our faith in Jesus Christ that He is enough.

00:14:58,130 --> 00:15:05,130
There's a story in the Bible of a woman who is bleeding for a decade or so and sick

00:15:05,130 --> 00:15:09,130
and it has been to her life savings going to doctors.

00:15:09,130 --> 00:15:13,130
And Jesus was walking through a crowd, being touched by everybody reaching out,

00:15:13,130 --> 00:15:15,130
wanting something from Him.

00:15:15,130 --> 00:15:17,130
Jesus, Jesus, heal me, heal me.

00:15:17,130 --> 00:15:21,130
The apostles, I can imagine, were pushing the peaked crowds back

00:15:21,130 --> 00:15:24,130
and a woman crawled underneath everybody and thought,

00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:30,130
if I could just touch his garment because he has everything I need.

00:15:30,130 --> 00:15:37,130
He is everything I need and she rubbed her hand along his garment as he walked by

00:15:37,130 --> 00:15:41,130
and healing went out from him and healed her.

00:15:41,130 --> 00:15:45,130
And it's crazy thing in the midst of this crowd.

00:15:45,130 --> 00:15:49,130
Jesus turns around to his apostles and says, who touched me?

00:15:49,130 --> 00:15:53,130
I'm sure the apostles are like, are you freaking out of your mind?

00:15:53,130 --> 00:15:56,130
Lord, I mean everybody's touching you.

00:15:56,130 --> 00:15:58,130
We're smashed in this crowd.

00:15:58,130 --> 00:15:59,130
Everybody's screaming.

00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:01,130
What do you mean who touched you?

00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:03,130
What do you mean who touched you?

00:16:03,130 --> 00:16:05,130
Somebody touched me.

00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,130
Somebody touched me.

00:16:06,130 --> 00:16:07,130
And he turns around.

00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:08,130
Who touched me?

00:16:08,130 --> 00:16:09,130
Who touched me?

00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:11,130
And here, left out the crowd.

00:16:11,130 --> 00:16:14,130
This is woman, crouched, looking up.

00:16:14,130 --> 00:16:16,130
Shy.

00:16:16,130 --> 00:16:18,130
Uninvited.

00:16:18,130 --> 00:16:21,130
I'm wondering, am I going to get yelled at?

00:16:21,130 --> 00:16:24,130
She said, Lord, it was I.

00:16:24,130 --> 00:16:28,130
And he said, your faith has healed you.

00:16:28,130 --> 00:16:31,130
Does that mean your faith in being healed?

00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:35,130
Does that mean your faith in being cured?

00:16:35,130 --> 00:16:36,130
I don't believe so.

00:16:36,130 --> 00:16:41,130
I believe it was her faith in Jesus Christ.

00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:48,130
Her faith that he was everything he was all she needed.

00:16:48,130 --> 00:16:53,130
Whether she was going to be healed or not, she was all.

00:16:53,130 --> 00:16:55,130
He was all she needed.

00:16:55,130 --> 00:16:57,130
And that's where we need to be.

00:16:57,130 --> 00:16:59,130
God is all I need.

00:16:59,130 --> 00:17:02,130
Whether I get healed or I don't get healed.

00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:04,130
It's not about this world.

00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:06,130
This is not my home.

00:17:06,130 --> 00:17:08,130
I want to go home.

00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:09,130
I long for eternity.

00:17:09,130 --> 00:17:12,130
I long to spend eternity in heaven.

00:17:12,130 --> 00:17:17,130
Just getting to know my Savior more and more forever and ever and ever.

00:17:18,130 --> 00:17:22,130
That's how vast the knowledge of God is.

00:17:22,130 --> 00:17:31,130
None of us can even understand or grasp the depth with the breath of the knowledge of God

00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:33,130
that we're going to gain in eternity.

00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:35,130
That's what I long for.

00:17:35,130 --> 00:17:37,130
Yes, do I want to be healed?

00:17:37,130 --> 00:17:38,130
Sure.

00:17:38,130 --> 00:17:42,130
Do I want to spend some time with my grandkids and my children and my wife?

00:17:42,130 --> 00:17:43,130
Absolutely.

00:17:44,130 --> 00:17:47,130
But not more than I want to spend with my Savior.

00:17:47,130 --> 00:17:51,130
And if it is ever more than I want to spend with my Savior,

00:17:51,130 --> 00:17:54,130
they are an idol in my life.

00:17:54,130 --> 00:17:57,540
And Lord, may that never be.

00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:59,540
That needs to be our prayer.

00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:04,540
Lord, make you all I need, Heavenly Father.

00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:10,540
Just whatever you need to put me through so that you are all I need

00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:14,540
and you are by desire of my heart.

00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:17,540
Lord, we thank You in Jesus' name.

00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:18,540
Amen.

